  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/misc5/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. 2026-11-01 review @100b6fbb6e: newline-terminated fixtures: c.js 2 lines -> 1-3, gradlew (bash) 3 -> 1-4, a.php 2 -> 1-3, a.pl 2 -> 1-3 (wrong). Python (py.py len(splitlines()), and the synthesizer's _read_file_end_line), Java, Ruby, C, Go, Rust, Kotlin and Swift are exact. So the item's Python examples do not reproduce. The 4-line C shift did not reproduce: tmate's server-fn.c gives server_destroy_pane 293-341, which is exact. The original tmux file is not here. Separately, lua.py emits its file node as 1-1. MECHANISM: file-node end_line taken from tree.root_node.end_point[0]+1, which is one past the last line when the grammar's root ends at (N,0) after a trailing newline. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: none."  # 6ff7
